\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Simulation of UP-DOWN states, effect of serotonin and coupling strength. (a) Global circuit model illustration. (b) Connectivity matrix for the global circuit and DRN prejections. (c) Replication of UP and DOWN state dynamics. Without any serotonin stimulation, the activity in the brain regions UP and DOWN states. (d) Serotonin stimulation induces a DOWN state in several regions. Probability values between 0.5-1 seconds after the serotonin stimulation onset are included. (e) Direct statistical test of the DOWN state probability during serotonin stimulation. (f) All four options of modelling serotonin stimulation, averaged over all regions in the network. The first letter in the legend description is the population targeted by serotonin, the sign after it indicates the charge direction of the current to that population. (g) Difference between targeting E with an excitatory current and targeting I with an inhibitory current. (h) Down state probability by region in the 'I-' simulation.}}{5}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:resultsummary1}{{3}{5}{Simulation of UP-DOWN states, effect of serotonin and coupling strength. (a) Global circuit model illustration. (b) Connectivity matrix for the global circuit and DRN prejections. (c) Replication of UP and DOWN state dynamics. Without any serotonin stimulation, the activity in the brain regions UP and DOWN states. (d) Serotonin stimulation induces a DOWN state in several regions. Probability values between 0.5-1 seconds after the serotonin stimulation onset are included. (e) Direct statistical test of the DOWN state probability during serotonin stimulation. (f) All four options of modelling serotonin stimulation, averaged over all regions in the network. The first letter in the legend description is the population targeted by serotonin, the sign after it indicates the charge direction of the current to that population. (g) Difference between targeting E with an excitatory current and targeting I with an inhibitory current. (h) Down state probability by region in the 'I-' simulation}{figure.caption.5}{}}
